# Review responsibility for CMS-created pull requests.
#
# Decap CMS has no per-collection permissions: anyone who can sign in can open
# any collection and draft changes to it. This file is what actually gates
# publishing. With editorial_workflow on, every CMS edit opens a pull request,
# GitHub requests the owner of each changed path as reviewer, and branch
# protection on main requires that review before the pull request can merge.
#
# This is review responsibility, not access control. It stops a section going
# live unreviewed; it does not stop someone drafting a change to it.

# Insights articles and the insights listing. Add each editor as an owner of
# the section they are responsible for, so their colleagues' pull requests
# need their approval:
#   content/insights/**  @mwamer @editor-username
content/insights/**  @mwamer

# The CMS panel itself. A change to the admin configuration or the OAuth proxy
# should never land on an editor's commit without a deliberate review.
static/admin/**  @mwamer
oauth-proxy/**  @mwamer
hugo.toml  @mwamer
layouts/insights/**  @mwamer
layouts/partials/**  @mwamer
